S1. THE TWO DEEP-NEWTONIAN TAILS, DERIVED SYMBOLICALLY (this is the whole result)
======================================================================================================
    alpha=1:  lim (x - y)       = 1/2      => a - g = a0 * 1/2
    alpha=2:  lim y*(x - y)     = 1/2      => a - g = a0/(2y) = a0^2/(2g)
  [OK  ] alpha=1 leaves a CONSTANT offset a - g = a0/2 (limit 1/2), so the fractional anomaly is A_1 = a0/(2g) -- exactly the expression section 2 of the frozen pre-registration uses
  [OK  ] alpha=2 leaves a DECAYING offset a - g = a0^2/(2g) (limit of y(x-y) is 1/2), so the fractional anomaly is A_2 = a0^2/(2 g^2) -- one power of a0/g SMALLER

    A_2 / A_1 = 1/y = a0/g   <-- the collapse factor, and it is exact
  [OK  ] MUTATION: applying the alpha=2 diagnostic y*(x-y) to the alpha=1 closure DIVERGES, so the diagnostic genuinely distinguishes the two tails and is not satisfied by both

