VERDICT
======================================================================================================
  RESULT 1 -- AND IT IS THE MOST CONSEQUENTIAL FINDING OF THE DAY.
  Section 2 of the FROZEN DR4 pre-registration computes the s^TX SME boost-dipole amplitude
  from A = a0/(2|g_orb|), which is the deep-Newtonian tail of the RETIRED alpha=1 closure.
  On the alpha=2 kernel in force since 2026-07-30 the tail is A = a0^2/(2 g^2), smaller by a
  factor a0/g = 1.4e-6 at Saturn. Consequently |s^TX| falls 8.68e-10 -> 1.26e-15 (canonical)
  and 1.048e-9 -> 1.83e-15 (alt), and the pre-registered margin goes from a LIVE 1.50x/1.24x
  to 1.03e6x/7.09e5x. THE SIGN IS UNCHANGED (the collapse factor is positive); only the
  amplitude dies.

  *** THIS IS DIFFERENT IN KIND FROM AMENDMENT 4, AND WORSE. *** Amendment 4 moved numbers
  without flipping any pre-registered outcome. This flips one: a test declared LIVE and
  FALSIFIABLE becomes untestable. So the alpha>=2 switch, which cured the 1278x ephemeris
  liability at a cost of 0.0033 dex on SPARC, ALSO destroys the s^TX front as a falsifier.
  That cost was not priced when the switch was made and it is being priced now.
  AN AMENDMENT IS OWED. Only Carl may file it. Nothing frozen was edited here.

  RESULT 2 -- THE as-MG ROW IS CLEAN. No correction is owed. mu and nu are exact reciprocals
  across the closure (nu*mu = 1 identically, both kernels), so a prescription written as
  mu(a_ex/a0) legitimately takes the OBSERVED argument and is not nu fed the wrong one. The
  mutation control confirms argument choice DOES matter for nu -- just not for mu. Amendment
  4's 'may not be assumed sound' flag is discharged, and a clean bill of health is reported
  with the same emphasis a bug would have been.

  WHAT REMAINS UNDONE, and it is undone because of a spend limit rather than a judgement:
  the dSph likelihood with Upsilon profiled per object, the stars-vs-gas curve pair that
  would firm the screening leg's soft ~3%, and the m=2 bar signature with Omega_p and eps
  primary-sourced. None was attempted; none should be assumed to point either way.

  NOT CLAIMED: that a0 is derived (kappa = 1/2 stays FITTED); that the pincer moved (Theorem 3
  forbids all local L, Theorem 8's argument mismatch stands); that the theory is closed.
